  "AI content payment is not merely a copyright or transaction-efficiency problem; it is a question of political-economic legitimacy. As AI valuations reach hundreds of billions, society asks why the gains from public web content and human knowledge accrue to a few firms. The paper proposes a six-layer tiered data market — from free public content through scarce verified datasets to public benefit-sharing — and defines the AI network democratic economy: rights, pricing, participation, auditability, and returns, each democratized through machine-readable protocols like AICR/AICL.": "Il pagament per cuntegn IA n'è betg simplamain in problem da dretg d'autur u dad efficienza da transacziun; el è ina dumonda da legitimità politic-economica. Cun las valitaziuns da la IA che rajunschan tschientaners da milliardas, la societad dumonda pertge ils gudogns dal cuntegn public dal web e dal savair uman restan concentrads en paucas interpresas. L'artitgel proponia in martgà da datas graduà en sis nivels — da cuntegn public gratuit tras datasets verifitgads e raras enfin la participaziun dal public a l'utilitad — e definescha l'economia democratica da la rait da IA: dretgs, fixaziun da pretschs, participaziun, revisibilitad e rendiment, mintga vult democratisà tras protocols leschibels per maschinas sco AICR/AICL.",
